GNU QUIC NEWS - history of user-visible changes.

* Noteworthy changes in release ?.? (????-??-??) [?]

** Initial development.  No release has been made.
** QUIC connections (conn.h) and streams (stream.h, ranges.h): the
handshake, packet number spaces, ACKs, RTT estimation, loss detection and
probe timeouts and NewReno congestion control with persistent
congestion (RFC 9002), stream and
connection flow control, connection IDs, key update, idle timeout,
connection close and stateless reset; tested against quiche in both
directions, with loss.
** DTLS 1.2 (dtls12.h, dtls12cookie.h): the TLS 1.2 profile over datagrams,
with whole-flight retransmission and a stateless HelloVerifyRequest;
tested against OpenSSL, GnuTLS and wolfSSL.
** DTLS 1.3 (dtls.h, dtlscookie.h): the TLS 1.3 engine over datagrams with
record number encryption, fragmentation, ACKs, retransmission, KeyUpdate
and a stateless address-validating cookie; tested against wolfSSL.
** TLS 1.2 (tls12.h, tls12conn.h) with the same restricted profile as
Gumdrop and Hopf: ECDHE on secp256r1 and AEAD suites only, mandatory
extended master secret and renegotiation indication, ticket resumption.
